Tom: I really like hip-hop. The strong beat makes me want to move.
Anna: I see. For me it''s classical music. It makes me feel calm and peaceful.
Tom: Calm? When do you usually listen to it?
Anna: When I''m studying. It helps me concentrate. What about you?
Tom: I play hip-hop when I exercise, because it gives me energy.
Anna: That makes sense. Different music for different moods.', 'Anna 问 Tom 喜欢什么音乐;Tom 喜欢嘻哈,强节拍让他想动;Anna 喜欢古典乐,让她平静;她学习时听以助专注;Tom 锻炼时放嘻哈来提神;两人都觉得不同心情配不同音乐。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What kind of music does Tom like?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Hip-hop.","Classical music.","Country music.","Folk songs."]},{"q":"Why does Tom like that music?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It is the quietest.","Its strong beat makes him want to move.","His teacher chose it.","It is the oldest."]},{"q":"How does classical music make Anna feel?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Calm and peaceful.","Angry and tired.","Bored and sleepy.","Afraid and alone."]},{"q":"When does Anna usually listen to her favourite music?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["When she is dancing.","When she is studying.","When she is eating.","When she is sleeping."]},{"q":"Why does Tom play his music while exercising?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It makes him sleepy.","It is required by the gym.","It gives him energy.","It has no beat."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U5');
The aim of the festival is to raise money for charity.
Anyone who can sing or play an instrument may try out as a performer.
Students who think they have no musical talent can still help in other ways.
You can sell tickets, run a food stand, or set up the equipment before the show.', '通知:校园音乐节将于下月在运动场举办;目的是为慈善筹款;会唱歌或演奏乐器的人都可报名当表演者;觉得自己没有音乐天赋的同学也能帮忙;可以卖票、经营食品摊,或在演出前架设设备。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where will the music festival be held?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["In a city theatre.","At the train station.","In a shopping mall.","On the school sports field."]},{"q":"What is the aim of the festival?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To raise money for charity.","To sell instruments.","To choose a new teacher.","To close the school."]},{"q":"Who can try out as a performer?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only the teachers.","Anyone who can sing or play an instrument.","Only famous singers.","Nobody at all."]},{"q":"What can students without musical talent do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Stay at home.","Stop the festival.","Help with tickets, food or equipment.","Only watch quietly."]},{"q":"Which task is mentioned for volunteers?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Writing new songs.","Painting the field.","Driving a bus.","Setting up the equipment."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U5');
Mia: Don''t worry. Real progress is gradual; nobody plays well after one week.
Ben: So what should I do?
Mia: Try practising a little every day instead of one long session.
Ben: That''s a good idea. Anything else?
Mia: Record yourself playing, then listen and find your mistakes.
Ben: I see. So I can hear what to fix.
Mia: Exactly. Little by little, you''ll get much better.', 'Ben 学吉他很吃力,手指不够快;Mia 说进步是渐进的,没人一周就弹好;建议每天练一点,而非一次练很久;还建议录下自己演奏再听、找出错误;一点点就会进步很多。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What problem does Ben have?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["His fingers won''t move fast enough on the guitar.","He has lost his guitar.","He dislikes all music.","He cannot find a teacher."]},{"q":"What does Mia say about progress?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It happens in one week.","It is gradual and takes time.","It never happens.","It needs no practice."]},{"q":"What is Mia''s first piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Give up the guitar.","Practise once a month.","Practise a little every day.","Only watch others play."]},{"q":"What is Mia''s second piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Play as loudly as possible.","Never listen to himself.","Buy a new guitar.","Record himself and find mistakes."]},{"q":"What does Mia promise will happen little by little?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Ben will get much better.","Ben will quit.","His guitar will break.","Nothing will change."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U5');
Each member records a video of themselves singing alone at home.
All the videos are uploaded and joined into one performance online.
Anyone with a camera and the Internet can take part, from anywhere.
In this way, a virtual choir connects ordinary people into one global community.', '虚拟合唱团让相隔甚远的人也能一起唱;每位成员在家独自录下唱歌的视频;所有视频被上传并合成一段网络演出;任何有摄像头和网络的人都能参加;这样虚拟合唱团把普通人联结成一个全球社区。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does a virtual choir let people do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Buy cheaper instruments.","Sing together even when far apart.","Stop singing forever.","Travel to other countries."]},{"q":"How does each member take part?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["By singing on a real stage.","By writing a letter.","By recording a video alone at home.","By calling a teacher."]},{"q":"What happens to all the videos?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["They are deleted.","They are sold in shops.","They are kept secret.","They are joined into one online performance."]},{"q":"Who can take part in a virtual choir?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Anyone with a camera and the Internet.","Only professional singers.","Only one country.","Only children."]},{"q":"What does a virtual choir connect ordinary people into?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["One small village.","One global community.","One music shop.","One school class."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U5');
Sam: Do you prefer a stringed instrument or a wind instrument?
Lucy: What''s the difference exactly?
Sam: A stringed instrument, like the violin, makes sound from its strings. A wind one, like the flute, needs air.
Lucy: I think I''d rather try something with strings.
Sam: Then how about the guitar? It''s a good choice for a beginner.
Lucy: Great idea. I''ll start with the guitar.', 'Lucy 想学乐器但拿不定主意;Sam 问她偏好弦乐还是管乐;Lucy 问两者区别;Sam 解释弦乐(如小提琴)靠琴弦发声,管乐(如长笛)靠空气;Lucy 更想试弦乐;Sam 建议吉他适合初学者;Lucy 决定从吉他学起。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is Lucy''s problem at the start?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["She has no money.","She dislikes music.","She can''t decide which instrument to learn.","She lost her violin."]},{"q":"How does a stringed instrument make sound?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["By pushing air through it.","By being struck like a drum.","By staying silent.","From its strings."]},{"q":"What kind of instrument is the flute, according to Sam?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A wind instrument.","A stringed instrument.","A drum.","An electric one."]},{"q":"Which kind does Lucy prefer to try?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A wind instrument.","Something with strings.","A drum.","An electric keyboard."]},{"q":"Which instrument does Lucy finally choose?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["The flute.","The bagpipes.","The guitar.","The drums."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U5');
Try letting music change your mood for a few minutes.
A happy song can give you energy when you feel low.
A quiet piece can bring you relief after a hard day.
Whatever you are feeling, the right music can somehow make it a little better.', '给感到疲惫或难过的人一个小建议:试着让音乐花几分钟改变你的心情;低落时,一首欢快的歌能给你能量;辛苦一天后,一段安静的曲子能带来宽慰;无论你有什么感受,合适的音乐总能让它变好一些。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who is this idea for?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only music teachers.","Only famous singers.","Only small children.","Anyone who feels tired or sad."]},{"q":"What can a happy song do when you feel low?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Give you energy.","Make you more tired.","Stop you sleeping.","Take away your money."]},{"q":"What can a quiet piece bring after a hard day?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["More stress.","Relief.","A loud noise.","A new problem."]},{"q":"How long does the speaker suggest letting music change your mood?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["For many hours.","For a whole week.","For a few minutes.","For a whole day."]},{"q":"What is the speaker''s main message?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Music is a waste of time.","Only sad songs are useful.","You should never listen to music.","The right music can somehow make your mood better."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U5');

